+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `billing/invoice.py`:
+  - `Line.vat` now uses `net * rate` (it used `unit_price * rate`, so quantity was ignored). PRICING.md rule 3.
+  - `Invoice.add` raises `ValueError` immediately for a rate name not in `RATES`. PRICING.md rule 3.
+- `tests/test_invoice.py`: changed `test_reduced_rate_small_item`. It expected VAT 0.02 and gross 0.52 for 0.50 at the reduced rate. 0.50 × 0.05 = 0.025, which rule 4 says rounds half up to 0.03, so gross is 0.53. I believe the old test was wrong and updated it.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest` before the change: 4 of 6 tests failed.
+- `python -m unittest` after the change: 6 tests ran, all OK.
+- I checked the other test expectations by hand against PRICING.md. They match.
+
+## Not verified / notes
+- `docs/PRICING.md` was not changed. If finance meant 0.02 for the sticker case, the rule text would need to change, and that is their decision.
+- The rounding and Decimal(str()) paths are covered only by the existing tests. I added no new ones.
